
Developer tools:
  flint api <method> <path>                                         Call a Flint public API route
  flint api-request-logs get <api_request_log_id>                   Get API request log
  flint api-request-logs list                                       List API request logs
  flint auth import                                                 Manually import and validate a Flint API key
  flint auth login                                                  Sign in through the Flint website (recommended for local development)
  flint auth logout                                                 Revoke the active OAuth session and delete the active profile
  flint auth reauth                                                 Change authorized contexts or add scopes in the browser
  flint auth status                                                 Fetch the current credential context from the API without using cached metadata
  flint auth token                                                  Export an OAuth or workload identity access token as JSON
  flint completion <shell>                                          Print an offline bash, zsh, or fish completion script
  flint config get                                                  Print resolved Flint CLI configuration and saved profiles
  flint config set <key> <value>                                    Set profile or merchant guard configuration
  flint config unset <key>                                          Clear a saved profile setting
  flint config validate                                             Validate global and project Flint configuration
  flint context list                                                List authorized contexts and the active selection
  flint context switch [<context_id>]                               Choose the active merchant and environment
  flint demo-sessions create                                        Create demo session
  flint demo-sessions reset <demo_session_id>                       Reset demo session
  flint doctor                                                      Check credential, connectivity, scopes, and API compatibility; explain scopes that need a live key
  flint help [<topic>...]                                           Show command help or an offline reference topic
  flint help search <query>...                                      Find commands, webhook events, and reference topics offline
  flint history                                                     List or clear recent Flint resource IDs
  flint init                                                        Write or validate .flint/config.json project guards; commit this file with your project
  flint listen                                                      Forward Flint webhook events to a local endpoint using the local HMAC listen secret, regardless of endpoint signing methods. Delivery is at-least-once and uses the caller's API version. To test JWT, use a tunnel and a registered sandbox endpoint
  flint mcp serve                                                   Discover and run Flint operations with five MCP tools over stdio (UTF-8 JSON, string or safe integer request IDs). Uses the CLI credential: FLINT_API_KEY, the FLINT_PROFILE (or --profile) profile, or a saved flint login
  flint openapi get                                                 Get OpenAPI spec
  flint partner-app-installs list                                   List installed partner apps
  flint partner-app-installs revoke <partner_app_install_id>        Remove connected partner app
  flint partner-apps create                                         Create partner app
  flint partner-apps credentials create <partner_app_id>            Create partner app credential
  flint partner-apps credentials delete <partner_app_id> <partner_app_credential_id> Remove partner app credential
  flint partner-apps credentials get <partner_app_id> <partner_app_credential_id> Get partner app credential
  flint partner-apps credentials list <partner_app_id>              List partner app credentials
  flint partner-apps delete <partner_app_id>                        Delete partner app
  flint partner-apps get <partner_app_id>                           Get partner app
  flint partner-apps installs environment-grants revoke <partner_app_id> <partner_app_install_id> <environment_grant_id> Revoke environment grant
  flint partner-apps installs get <partner_app_id> <partner_app_install_id> Get partner app install
  flint partner-apps installs list <partner_app_id>                 List partner app installs
  flint partner-apps installs revoke <partner_app_id> <partner_app_install_id> Revoke partner app install
  flint partner-apps list                                           List partner apps
  flint partner-apps rotate-secret <partner_app_id>                 Rotate partner app secret
  flint partner-apps update <partner_app_id>                        Update partner app
  flint resource-timelines get <resource_id>                        Get a resource timeline
  flint schema command <command>...                                 Describe one command from the embedded API snapshot, without a request
  flint schema commands [<prefix>...]                               List command schemas, optionally only those under a command group
  flint schema errors                                               List CLI and public API error types and exit codes
  flint schema events [<event_type>]                                List webhook event types, or print payload schemas for a type or prefix
  flint schema input <command>...                                   Print the full JSON Schema of a command's --input body, including variants
  flint schema output <command>...                                  Print a command output JSON Schema
  flint signup                                                      Create an account and sandbox key. Without a code, email a verification code and save progress; finish with --verification-code. MCP and --no-input use two calls.
  flint support open                                                Start a Flint Help thread with your terminal context prefilled. Opens the composer in your browser; posting happens there.
  flint test-clocks advance <test_clock_id>                         Advance a test clock
  flint test-clocks create                                          Create a test clock
  flint test-clocks delete <test_clock_id>                          Archive a test clock
  flint test-clocks get <test_clock_id>                             Get a test clock
  flint test-clocks list                                            List test clocks
  flint trigger [<event_type>]                                      Create sandbox resources that produce a webhook event; no automatic cleanup (reset the sandbox when done)
  flint upgrade                                                     Upgrade Flint CLI to the latest stable release
  flint version                                                     Print CLI and public API schema version metadata

